  owner: pm-gh1461
body: "Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1461\n\n## Problem (pm 2026.10.13)\nAn extension command group (`registerCommand` with subcommands) declared its flags as `{ long: '--repo <value>', type: 'string', description: … }`, embedding the value placeholder in `long`. The SDK accepts that silently, and `pm <group> <sub> --help` then renders:\n\n```text\nOptions:\n  --repo <value> <value>    Repository owner/name\n  --pr <value> <value>      Positive pull request number\n  --reason <value> <value>  Durable decision reasoning\n  ...\nExtension-provided flags:\n  --commit <value>  Commit SHA implementing or explaining this decision\n  --pr <value>  Positive pull request number\n  --reason <value>  Durable decision reasoning\n  --repo <value>  Repository owner/name\n```\n\nTwo separate issues:\n1. **Placeholder doubling:** the host appends `<value>` to a `long` that already contains one. The supported form, `long: '--repo'` with `value_name: 'value'` (used by pm-lint), renders correctly, but nothing tells the author that the other form is wrong.\n2. **Duplicate listing for subcommand flags:** every subcommand flag appears twice, once under `Options:` and again under `Extension-provided flags:`, which costs agents tokens on every `--help` read. A top-level extension command (pm-lint's `pm lint --help`) lists its flags only once.\n\nSeen in unbraind/pm-review (a fleet package), `pm review verdict --help`.\n\n## Proposal\n- In `defineCommand` / `registerCommand` validation, either reject a `long` containing whitespace or `<…>` with a fix hint (`use long: '--repo', value_name: 'value'`), or normalize it into `long` + `value_name`.\n- Render each subcommand flag once. If the \"Extension-provided flags\" section adds information (provenance), merge it into the single listing instead of repeating every flag.\n\n\nImplementation intent\n\nPreserve the explicitly supported legacy inline-placeholder flag syntax while making placeholder arity and canonical option identity consistent across registration, help, contracts and real invocation."
